; An inner program for the singleton wrapper: one key owns the state.
;
; The wrapper runs this program over the coin's own data consed onto
; the inner solution, so the environment is (OWNER_KEY OWN . ARGS)
; once OWNER_KEY is curried. The owner signs the next inner program's
; hash, the next coin's amount, the extra conditions, and the
; spending transaction's outputs hash, bound to the singleton coin's
; own outpoint, so an authorization fits exactly one spend of exactly
; one coin. The outputs hash is sealed: the wrapper can claim the
; child and its state output but cannot place them, and the seal is
; what makes the signed placement immutable while leaving the input
; side open for anyone's fee input. The odd-amount CREATE_OUTPUT is
; the wrapper's child marker, rewritten by the wrapper into the next
; singleton coin and its state output. NEXT_AMOUNT of -113 ends the
; lineage. EXTRA_CONDITIONS pass through the wrapper unchanged: they
; may create only even-amount outputs, and none tagged with this
; lineage.
(program (OWNER_KEY (LAUNCHER MY_OUTPOINT MY_SPK MY_AMOUNT MY_INNER_HASH)
          NEXT_INNER_HASH NEXT_AMOUNT EXTRA_CONDITIONS OUTPUTS_HASH SIG)
  (c (list ASSERT_SIG_MY_OUTPOINT OWNER_KEY
           (sha256tree (list NEXT_INNER_HASH NEXT_AMOUNT EXTRA_CONDITIONS
                             OUTPUTS_HASH))
           SIG)
  (c (list SEAL_OUTPUTS OUTPUTS_HASH)
  (c (list CREATE_OUTPUT NEXT_INNER_HASH NEXT_AMOUNT)
     EXTRA_CONDITIONS))))
